SWEET WLAN re-join after an AP loss (patch 0282, W-D6 boot B, branch wlan/rejoin; docs/research/W-D6-rejoin-dhcp.md s.3 and 6 steps 5-7). Builds on 0281 (live event decode, link-down detector, DOWN to iOS). (1) KEPT SECRETS (user decision 2026-11-10): the hook copies the PMK, the join payload (and the four security values wpa_auth, wsec, auth, mfp) and the boot RSNEs into one RAM struct sw_rj (struct swl25_rj, sweet_wlan_l25_hs.h) before the L25 disarm and the init scrub wipe them; it is never printed or written anywhere else and is zeroed when the engine dies (sw_keep_end: poll thread ends, hand-over refused; sw_keep_abort). If it is missing when the link is lost, `WIFI GAP: keep rejoin: the link is DOWN but the join payload and PMK are not kept`. (2) STATE MACHINE in the keep thread (swl25_rj_step, one call per pass under the en0 lock; the only user of the engine): UP -> DOWN (the 0281 detector) -> JOINING -> KEYING -> UP. First attempt when DOWN is entered, then 2, 4, 8, 16, 30 s (cap) for ever (swg_rj_backoff_ms); one line per attempt `SWEET WLAN: keep rejoin attempt N`, `SWEET WLAN: keep rejoin UP after N attempts, T ms` when done. An attempt reads back wpa_auth, wsec, auth, mfp (GET_VAR) and re-sends only what differs from the boot join, then sends the kept `join` (SET_VAR, the same 76 B v1 payload with the wildcard BSSID) and waits at most SWG_J_BUDGET_MS (10 s) for SET_SSID 0 + LINK up (the events are noted by swg_ke_note), then reads WLC_GET_BSSID and the association-request RSNE, sets up the supplicant with the kept PMK and switches the EAPOL divert on. (3) LIVE 4-WAY: wlan_en0.h en0_rx_deliver hands ethertype 0x888E frames to the hook en0->eapol (swl25_rj_eapol -> swj_rx, the boot code); the M2/M4 reply is posted on the flow ring by en0_tx_frame; outside KEYING EAPOL is dropped with a counted GAP (`WIFI GAP: EN4 EAPOL frame dropped`). After M4 has left (tx completion or 200 ms) wsec_key pairwise + group and the wsec merge are sent (a refusal fails the attempt, it does not stop the engine), BSSID/chanspec/RSSI are read (swl25_live), then the thread tells iOS outside the lock: sweet_wlan_a80211_kept_up (new BSSID/channel/RSSI, kept.joined, ASSOC_DONE result 0 = kev 9, 2, 3, 4 with isLinkDown 0) and en0_link_only(e, 1) (IFF_RUNNING, KEV_DL_LINK_ON, so configd re-runs DHCP). The RSSI refresh is skipped while an attempt is JOINING or KEYING. The 0281 `link UP event ignored` GAP now fires only outside an attempt. (4) The store judge (sweet_wlan_l25_wl.h, 17 rows) gets seven rows: SET join (content bound: SSID_len 1..32, reserved fields exact, BSSID the wildcard or the known AP), SET wpa_auth / auth / mfp (one allowed value each), GET wpa_auth / auth / mfp (read-only). The headers (sweet_wlan_g2.h, sweet_wlan_l25_hs.h, sweet_wlan_l25_wl.h, sweet_wlan_radio.h, sweet_wlan_en0.h, sweet_wlan_a80211.c) are regenerated in place in patches 0174, 0206, 0201 and 0199 from shim/ (tools/gen-wlan-hunks, tools/gen-wlan-en0-patch, tools/gen-wlan-a80211-patch); this patch holds the hand-written glue hunks of sweet_wlan.c. NEW firmware-facing commands: SET_VAR join (live), SET_VAR wpa_auth / auth / mfp / wsec (only when the read-back differs), GET_VAR wpa_auth / auth / mfp, and the existing wsec_key x2 + wsec GET/SET + GET_BSSID/chanspec/RSSI/assoc_info/assoc_req_ies in a new use after the hand-over. Not run on hardware. Review 0282 fixes (Opus, rule 8): a SOFT stop inside any re-join ioctl is cleared by swl25_rj_step itself (re-join off for the boot, sw_rj and the supplicant wiped, one `WIFI GAP: keep rejoin disabled: soft stop in <step>`), a loss event during JOINING/KEYING fails the attempt, an M1 after an accepted M3 is dropped, the M4 counts as sent only when en0 posted it (the thread passes e->eapol_last_ok), secret leftovers are wiped (payload shadow, swj_rx stack). Round 2: the glue passes SWL25_RJ_BUSY_ARG(&sw_rj, en0_tx_busy(...)) (not gated on m4_seen: the 200 ms M4 wait is back), a stop raised by the re-join's ring-2 drain is not cleared (the keep loop ends on it), a stop before the ioctl completion is noted with a GAP.
